  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Volume is contained within a cardboard slip case covered in white fish net, decorated with color and black and white illustrations depicting a dragonfly and flowers. The back of the case displays a cardboard illustration of the Vigia lamp and the collection name. The cover of the volume is white with the image of a woman's eyes and cardboard illustration of a flower within a tear. The back cover also depicts cardboard illustrations of flowers and lily pads. The pages are decorated with illustrations, both in black and white and color. Text is a selection from Randall's book "The rhizome as a field of broken bones" presented in both English and Spanish.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Part of a collection of handmade chapbooks, most with cords for hanging (literatura de cordel), published by Ediciones Vigía under the auspices of the Cuban Ministry of Culture.</subfield>
  </datafield>
